  "title": "Chocolate-dipped lebkuchen",
  "subtitle": "German spiced honey biscuits dipped in dark chocolate",
  "excerpt": "Lebkuchen are soft, richly spiced German Christmas biscuits made with honey, warm spices, and a little ground almond, then dipped in dark chocolate once cooled. They mature with keeping: baked lebkuchen stored in a tin with a slice of apple will soften over three to four days from their initially slightly chewy texture to something much more tender and fragrant. They are among the most characteristic flavours of a German Christmas market.",
