  "sourceType": "CLASSIC",
  "sourceNotes": "Lebkuchen have been made in the Nuremberg region of Bavaria since the 13th century; the Nuremberg Lebkuchen received EU Protected Geographical Indication status in 1996. The recipe type used here (Honiglebkuchen, honey lebkuchen) is the most widely made style at home, and follows the method documented in German baking references including Luisa Weiss's Classic German Baking (2016) and the Nuremberg Lebkuchen-Schmidt tradition.",
