  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Lebkuchen dough is made by warming honey, sugar, and butter together, then combining with the dry ingredients. It is a soft, sticky dough that needs chilling before rolling. The biscuits look pale and dry when they come out of the oven; this is correct. They firm up further as they cool and should not be browned. The chocolate dipping is done once fully cool and completely sets the surface."
          }
        ]
      },
