      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make the dough"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Combine {{honey}}, {{dark-brown-sugar}}, and {{unsalted-butter}} in a medium saucepan over a low heat. Stir until the butter melts and the sugar dissolves. Remove from the heat and leave to cool to room temperature, about 20 minutes. Stir in the beaten {{eggs}}. Sift {{plain-flour}}, {{ground-almonds}}, {{bicarbonate-of-soda}}, {{mixed-spice}}, {{cinnamon-ground}}, and {{cardamom-ground}} into the honey mixture, then add {{mixed-peel}} and mix to a soft, sticky dough. Wrap in cling film and refrigerate for 30 minutes."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Roll and bake"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Heat the oven to 175°C (conventional). Line two baking trays. Roll the chilled dough on a lightly floured surface to 5 mm thickness. Cut into 6 cm rounds or squares and transfer to the lined trays, spacing 2 cm apart. Bake for 12 to 14 minutes until the surface looks set and dry but the biscuits are still pale. They will firm significantly as they cool. Cool on a wire rack for at least 30 minutes."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Dip in chocolate"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Melt {{dark-chocolate}} in a heatproof bowl over barely simmering water. Dip the base of each completely cooled biscuit into the chocolate to a depth of about 8 mm, let the excess drip off, then place chocolate-side down on a sheet of baking paper. Alternatively, dip the entire biscuit and lay flat to set. Leave at room temperature for 1 to 2 hours until the chocolate is completely set."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
